From db2d86ab0c77e534a1b82fa16cf92b5184e3bcd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:52:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(capture): add zoom and pan to the annotation editor

The capture in the annotation editor now shows through a display-only
view transform layered on the fitted canvas: Ctrl+wheel zooms around the
pointer (0.5x-16x fit-relative), Ctrl+left-drag pans with a clamp that
keeps a visible slice on screen, and zoom-out/fit/zoom-in buttons step
the same view. Annotation geometry, rasterization and export stay in
canvas space, so delivered pixels are unchanged. The touchpad path
accumulates axis deltas at the InputArea scroll rate and the whole axis
stream is consumed while Ctrl is held. In live annotation only the ink
layers magnify (the desktop behind cannot), documented as a caveat.
Relayout keeps the zoom and re-clamps the pan; Live/Frozen switches
reset the view.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
