 Annotation tool keys (no modifier): **`m`** move, **`b`** brush, **`h`** highlighter, **`l`** line, **`a`** arrow, **`s`** rectangle, **`o`** circle, **`t`** text, **`n`** numbering, **`u`** blur, **`e`** eraser, **`c`** crop, **`z`** freeze (live overlay), **`p`** toggle the captured pointer, **`f`** cycle the shape fill through off, semi-transparent, and opaque, **`1`** to **`8`** pick the current tool's color from the eight swatches, **`[`** and **`]`** change the current tool's size. **`Ctrl+Z`** undoes, **`Ctrl+Shift+Z`** and **`Ctrl+Y`** redo, **`[keybinds].copy`** copies, **`[keybinds].save`** saves.
 
+The capture view zooms and pans without touching the recorded pixels: **`Ctrl`** and the mousewheel zoom around the pointer from half to sixteen times the fitted size, **`Ctrl`** and a left-drag pan the capture, and the zoom-out, fit, and zoom-in buttons in the toolbar step the same view and restore it. Panning is limited so part of the capture always stays on screen, and moving or resizing the toolbar never reflows the zoomed canvas. In live annotation the ink layers zoom while the live desktop behind them does not, so freeze with **`z`** first when the zoomed view must match the screen.
+
 The pointer button and **P** work the same in region, fullscreen, and frozen-screen editing. `[shell.screenshot].show_cursor` sets the initial choice; toggling does not change that setting. Only the pointer recorded inside the captured area can appear. Noctalia captures the cursor separately through `ext-image-copy-capture-v1` and composites it over the same cursor-free background for both choices. When separate cursor capture is unsupported or fails, the ordinary screenshot keeps the configured pointer choice, the button is disabled with an explanatory tooltip, and **P** shows the same explanation. In live annotation, freeze with **Z** first.
 
 **Exception**: window capture never includes the pointer, so `[shell.screenshot].show_cursor` applies only to region, fullscreen, and frozen-screen capture. The pointer button and **P** stay disabled for window capture.
